@page "/terms"

@* The terms, as the app works (moderation, plans, payments). A starting text: have it reviewed for the place the
   operator is established before launch (README, Privacy and terms). *@

<PageTitle>Terms · @Brand.AppName</PageTitle>

<article class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated @PrivacyPage.LastUpdated</p>

    <p>
        These terms are the agreement between you and @Brand.Operator ("we") for using @Brand.AppName. By creating an
        account or using the app, you accept them. Our <a href="privacy">privacy policy</a> explains what we do with
        your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>You need to be at least 13, or the age at which you can agree to this yourself where you live.</li>
        <li>Keep your sign-in details to yourself; you're responsible for what's done with your account.</li>
        <li>You can delete your account at any time in Settings. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these
            terms, and will tell you why unless the law or someone's safety prevents it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What you post</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Your comments, tips, insights and corrections stay yours. You let us show them in the app, to other users,
            for as long as they're up; that permission ends when you delete them or your account.</li>
        <li>Don't post anything unlawful, hateful, harassing, sexually explicit, or that infringes someone else's rights,
            and don't spam. Mark spoilers as spoilers.</li>
        <li>Posts are moderated. A post can be held for review (one with a link, for example), refused for blocked words,
            or hidden after other users flag it. When one of yours is hidden, you can still see it and why.</li>
        <li>Don't try to get around rate limits, read other people's data, or disrupt the service, including by automated
            means.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The show information and insights</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Show and episode data comes from <CatalogCredits />@(Brand.Catalog.Licence switch
            {
                CatalogLicence.Own => ", under its own licence. Quotes and some facts come",
                CatalogLicence.Invented => ", which is invented. Quotes and some facts come",
                _ => ", and quotes and some facts"
            }) from Wikiquote and Wikidata, under the
            <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY-SA</a> licence.
            Pictures belong to their owners.</li>
        <li>Insights, forecasts and recommendations are worked out from that data and can be wrong. They're
            for interest and planning, not promises: a forecast season may never come, and a "where to watch" link may
            have changed.</li>
        <li>Links to streaming services take you to their sites, under their own terms. Some carry an affiliate code, so
            the service may pay us for a sign-up; that never changes what we show you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Plans and payments</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Browsing the catalog needs no account. With a free account, following, tracking, ratings, lists and the
            basic insights are free. Pro and Family add the insights
            listed on the plan page, which can change over time; we'll tell you before a paid feature you have is taken
            out of your plan.</li>
        <li>A paid plan is a subscription, by the month or the year, at the price shown when you buy it, taken by our
            payment provider. It renews until you cancel.</li>
        <li>When you cancel, you keep the plan until the end of the period you've paid for, and nothing more is charged.
            We don't refund part-periods, except where the law gives you that right (for example a right to withdraw
            from a purchase within a set time).</li>
        <li>We may change prices; a new price applies from your next renewal after we've told you, and you can cancel
            before then.</li>
        <li>A Family plan's owner pays for up to five members, who get Pro while the owner's plan runs. When it ends,
            members go back to their own plans. What anyone made on a paid plan stays when the plan ends.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>We work to keep @Brand.AppName running and your data safe, but provide it as it is, without guarantees that it
            will always be available or free of errors. We may change, add or remove features.</li>
        <li>As far as the law allows, we aren't liable for indirect losses, or for more than you paid us in the twelve
            months before a claim. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer law that can't be
            waived.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
        We may update these terms; the date above says when. We'll tell you in the app before a change that affects you
        takes effect, and if you don't agree you can stop using the app and delete your account.
        These terms are governed by the law of the place where @Brand.Operator is established, without taking away the
        protection of the law where you live.
        @if (Brand.ContactEmail is { } email)
        {
            <span> Questions go to <a href="mailto:@email">@email</a>.</span>
        }
    </p>
</article>
